# {{projectName}}

{{#if (includes transports 'streamable')}}An Express-based {{/if}}MCP JavaScript SDK 2.0 server starter using the `2026-07-28` protocol{{#if (and (includes transports 'stdio') (includes transports 'streamable'))}} over stdio and Streamable HTTP{{else if (includes transports 'stdio')}} over stdio{{else}} over Streamable HTTP{{/if}}.

The built-in knowledge-base example demonstrates how the three server primitives work together:

1. Call the `search_documents` Tool to find one of three MCP guides.
2. Read the returned `kb://documents/{documentId}` Resource URI.
3. Get the `review_document` Prompt to review the same document.

The example is deterministic and has no external data dependency. Tool results include both
`structuredContent` and text content, resources are Markdown documents with stable URIs, and missing
resources return a protocol-level Resource Not Found error.
{{#if (includes transports 'streamable')}}

The HTTP endpoint uses `@modelcontextprotocol/express` with Express 5. Its default localhost binding
validates the `Host` header to protect local development servers from DNS rebinding.
{{/if}}

## Development

Requires Node.js 22 and npm 10. The repository's `.nvmrc`, `packageManager`, and lockfile define the
supported local and CI toolchain.

```bash
nvm use
npm install
{{#if (includes transports 'stdio')}}npm run dev:stdio{{else}}npm run dev:web{{/if}}
```
{{#if (includes transports 'streamable')}}

Run the Streamable HTTP transport on `http://localhost:8401/mcp`:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
npm run dev:web
```

The local `.env` file is ignored by Git. `PORT` and `--port` must resolve to an integer from `1` to `65535`.
{{/if}}

Run the same verification stages used by CI:

```bash
npm run check
```

The individual stages are also available as{{#if (includes plugins 'style')}} `npm run lint`,{{/if}} `npm run build`{{#if (includes plugins 'vitest')}},
`npm test`, and `npm run coverage`{{/if}}. The production build preserves the source module layout as
Node.js 22 ESM under `build`; `build/index.js` remains the executable entrypoint.

Inspect the npm package before publishing:

```bash
npm pack --dry-run
```

## Usage

```bash
{{#if (includes transports 'stdio')}}# Start with stdio transport{{#if (includes transports 'streamable')}} (default){{/if}}
node build/index.js
{{/if}}{{#if (includes transports 'streamable')}}
# Start with Streamable HTTP
node build/index.js web --port 8401
{{/if}}

# Print CLI help or the package version
node build/index.js --help
node build/index.js --version
```

## Environment Variables

{{#if (includes transports 'streamable')}}- `PORT`: Streamable HTTP port (default: `8401`)
{{/if}}- `NODE_ENV`: `production` for production builds or `local` for development
{{#if (includes plugins 'inspector')}}- `MCP_INSPECTOR_API_TOKEN`: optional stable token for the MCP Inspector development session
{{/if}}

